            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "This feels like it should be the first commit: the meson option, the log service. Maybe you are playing 4D chess that I don't understand. Haha. That said, I don't care, they just need to all merge together."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed. Building the route in reverse does seem a bit odd and makes reviewing a bit harder."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "How does one reverse the order without just squashing everything into a single patch?  The service needs the entries collection.  the entries collection needs the entries.  the entries need the attachment ... what am I missing?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "You could do an interactive rebase and 'just' reorder the commits. In the case of this series however I don't think it would be that trivial of a task and you probably would have to move some code around patches.\n\nAt least I was thinking about building the routes from the root, starting with /redfish/v1/{Systems/Manager}/LogServices/CPER and continue building the URI from there. \n\n> The service needs the entries collection.  the entries collection needs the entries.  the entries need the attachment\n\nI do understand where you are coming from, but the reverse is true aswell looking at redfish. Patch #1 implements the last segment of the URI - `/attachment` - whilst the LogService itself (`/redfish/v1/Systems/LogServices/CPER`) and any following resource haven't been implemented yet. \n\nI don't think it is as important, as long as all patches of the series go in together in one push as Gunnar has mentioned. Marking this as resolved, undo if there are objections."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Could you link the patch?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "the patches share the same gerrit topic as this patch.  Do you think the link is important enough to go in the commit message?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "I think the commit message is more important for providing context than gerrit. But I wouldn't mind not seeing the link in the message."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall in support of this series. The Redfish CPER support feels like it could use a little more standardization.. \n\nNeed access to Redfish but hoping Redfish could solve \nhttps://github.com/DMTF/Redfish/issues/6339"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "dead link? ^^"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "You need to be a DMTF member to get to that URL."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Aah I see, thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 93,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "We could enable later.. I know we want to enable by default as much function as possible but until cper is present and more stable might make sense to disable by default.. I always struggle enabling by default at this stage. That said, I don't care that much."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 93,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "IMO everything should be enabled by default in meson.options for CI coverage.  Enabling things by default here is not the same as enabling them by default in the yocto recipe.  You should raise this question again in the recipe review (where I will propose to enable it by default again \ud83e\udd23)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 93,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 95,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you expand this to be correct.. Paths are under systems if BMCWEB_REDFISH_EVENTLOG_LOCATION = system. I know other log service options don't have it correct but helps someone reading this option"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 95,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure, what does that look like?  Don't forget the manager name is also configurable (what goes in the ? field)\n\n Enable CPER log service transactions through Redfish.  Paths                     are under /redfish/v1/<BMCWEB_REDFISH_EVENTLOG_LOCATION>/<?>/LogServices/CPER."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 95,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 194,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Most of our LogServices have LogEntryTypes.. I think it is still Event in this case. Oh well. \n\n```\n       \"LogEntryTypes\": {           \n...\n            \"enumDescriptions\": {\n                \"CXL\": \"The log contains CXL log entries.\",\n                \"Event\": \"The log contains Redfish-defined messages.\",\n                \"Multiple\": \"The log contains multiple log entry types and, therefore, the log service cannot guarantee a single entry type.\",\n                \"OEM\": \"The log contains entries in an OEM-defined format.\",\n                \"SEL\": \"The log contains legacy IPMI System Event Log (SEL) entries.\"\n            },\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 194,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "But the type is placed on the LogEntry itself and not on the LogService right? The previous patch has the LogEntryType added on the entry"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 194,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I copy / pasted this from handleSystemsAndManagersEventLogServiceGet, which does not set LogEntryTypes.  I'm happy to set that to Event if that's useful/more complete."
                },
                {
